{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3281","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3281","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3281\",\"parent_revision\":\"ac0a5c0df09a1b1f86fac6e597cb892080e47e3c99388693f29f0765506a4278\",\"root_revision\":\"ac0a5c0df09a1b1f86fac6e597cb892080e47e3c99388693f29f0765506a4278\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Docs\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-28\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finalize.md`'s Output Validation Gate required-sections table has this row: `Priority` | Contains `Effort:` field.\\n\\nBut `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/swarm.md`'s groomer subsection list treats `Effort` as its own distinct section (`Reproducibility, Priority, Impact, Benefits, Expected Behavior, Acceptance Criteria, Files, Resources, Dependencies, Effort`), separate from `Priority`. finalize.md's required-sections table and its explicitly-listed optional sections (`Root-Cause Analysis, Impact, Benefits, Expected Behavior, Files, Resources, Dependencies, Scope, Decision`) never mention `Effort` at all \u2014 it is not validated as required, not validated as optional, and the `Priority` row's literal-text requirement (`Effort:`) does not describe where the groomer actually puts effort content.\\n\\nObserved live: grooming #3276, the groomer produced a well-formed `Effort` section (Small-to-Medium estimate with rationale) and a well-formed `Priority` section (P2 justification) as two separate sections, neither containing the literal substring `Effort:` inside `Priority`. The orchestrator judged this a stale/misplaced table row from an earlier iteration (when Priority and Effort may have been one combined section) and did not block the groom on it \u2014 but every future groom will re-hit this same ambiguous checkpoint and have to make the same judgment call.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: possible directions for grooming to evaluate, not requirements \u2014 (1) add `Effort` as its own required (or explicitly optional) row in finalize.md's table, and (2) fix the `Priority` row to describe what it actually validates rather than referencing a field that lives in a different section.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 2026-08-29, while grooming #3276 via /dh:work-backlog-item\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"5cdce83f6904bc6f97f1f36939f74e516e91928d93161ed1b54b009d2345d0a9\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRSB6VA\"}"}